{"id":1809,"date":"2025-04-01T17:00:00","date_gmt":"2025-04-01T17:00:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/?post_type=news&#038;p=1809"},"modified":"2025-04-01T17:30:29","modified_gmt":"2025-04-01T17:30:29","slug":"breaking-news-miskatonic-flood-alert","status":"publish","type":"news","link":"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/news\/breaking-news-miskatonic-flood-alert\/","title":{"rendered":"Breaking News: Miskatonic Flood Alert"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p><em>Breaking news from the <\/em>Arkham Advertiser<em>: read the front page news below, and download the PDF edition to read the whole issue. <\/em><\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><a href=\"https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/2025\/03\/The-Arkham-Advertiser-02-Fall-24.pdf\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/2025\/03\/Download-Button.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-989\" style=\"width:250px\"\/><\/a><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\" id=\"h-miskatonic-flood-alert\">MISKATONIC FLOOD ALERT!<\/h1>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"774\" src=\"https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/2025\/03\/Arkham-Advertiser-02-Fall-24_headlinephoto-1024x774.jpg\" alt=\"Miskatonic Flood Alert!\" class=\"wp-image-1691\" srcset=\"https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/image-converter\/2025\/03\/Arkham-Advertiser-02-Fall-24_headlinephoto-1024x774.webp 1024w, https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/image-converter\/2025\/03\/Arkham-Advertiser-02-Fall-24_headlinephoto-300x227.webp 300w, https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/image-converter\/2025\/03\/Arkham-Advertiser-02-Fall-24_headlinephoto-768x580.webp 768w, https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/image-converter\/2025\/03\/Arkham-Advertiser-02-Fall-24_headlinephoto.webp 1068w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" style=\"text-align: center;\" id=\"h-imminent-risk-to-life-city-wide-evacuation\">Imminent risk to life!<br>City-Wide Evacuation!<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p><em>Editor\u2019s Note: In light of the United States Weather Bureau announcement regarding the impending rainfall, Arkham City Hall has elected to use the <\/em>Arkham Advertiser<em> to provide information to our readers in the event of severe flooding and other environmental disasters. Please check daily for additional updates as this story develops.<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The United States Weather Bureau has forecast a series of intense storms to strike the Miskatonic River Valley throughout the next five to seven days, with expected rainfall ranging from \u00be inches to 2 inches per day. Total rainfall is expected to exceed 8 inches, with certain forecast models predicting over a foot of rain. These storms will be accompanied by heavy winds, intense lightning, and flash flooding throughout the region, particularly along the Miskatonic River. Citizens should expect downed trees and power lines, as well as other significant storm damage.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>If you are in any of the following areas, please evacuate immediately for higher ground:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><em>Arkham Merchant District, particularly areas along the River Docks<\/em><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><em>Rivertown, particularly River Street (near the Black Cave and the Arkham General Store)<\/em><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><em>The Woods near Uptown<\/em><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image wp-duotone-unset-1\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"830\" height=\"807\" src=\"https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/2025\/03\/Arkham-Advertiser-02-Fall-24_map.jpg\" alt=\"Flood map of Arkham City\" class=\"wp-image-1732\" srcset=\"https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/image-converter\/2025\/03\/Arkham-Advertiser-02-Fall-24_map.webp 830w, https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/image-converter\/2025\/03\/Arkham-Advertiser-02-Fall-24_map-300x292.webp 300w, https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/image-converter\/2025\/03\/Arkham-Advertiser-02-Fall-24_map-768x747.webp 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 830px) 100vw, 830px\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n<p>Other areas may be issued evacuation alerts based on the progress of the incoming storm and flood levels. Citizens with motorcars are encouraged not to drive as high water may result in vehicles being swept away in flash flood conditions.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Alderman Sarah Howells spoke regarding the severity of the impending storms,&nbsp; saying, \u201cOur citizens must realize the true danger that these flood waters represent to them as individuals. Please, for your own sake, get to higher ground, avoid high water areas, and keep your families safe. Your life is worth more than your business, your house, or your possessions. Those can be replaced. You cannot.\u201d<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>City Hall and Arkham City Police Department have established several safety stations, providing food, fresh water, medical supplies, and shelter for those displaced by the storm or evacuating because of the flood risk.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>These safety stations are at the following locations:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><em>South Church, Southside<\/em><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><em>Arkham Historical Society, Southside<\/em><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><em>Miskatonic University Student Union, Miskatonic University<\/em><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><em>The Palace Movie Theater, Downtown<\/em><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Arkham Fire Service, medical staff from St. Mary\u2019s Hospital, and Arkham City Police Department have already been stationed throughout the city.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>While located in a flood zone, Schoffner\u2019s General Store has also received extra stock shipments of food and supplies to help with storm relief efforts. Community members and those choosing to stay within the flood zones are also gathering here to disperse news and lend help.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>In the event of extreme flooding, citizens are encouraged to use major thoroughfares, especially if the roadway is cleared from floodwaters and debris. Recommend\u00adations include avoiding Water St., River St., Boundary St., and Aylesbury St., as well as other roadways running parallel to the Miskatonic River. Steer clear of crossing the river, in the event floodwaters overwhelm bridge supports holding up the roadways.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Regarding future repairs for those worried about property damage, Arkham Public Works Maintenance Supervisor Gregory Baerson noted, \u201cHigh winds, excessive rain, and flooding all have the capability to bring down even the largest trees. Leave clean up to the professionals, though. If you do have storm damage that requires an urgent remedy and are able to notify us, we\u2019ll do our best to make our way to you as soon as possible. We expect a big job, but we\u2019re up to the task.\u201d<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Residents are advised to look for city notices posted at City Hall and the shelter locations.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Further updates will be provided by the <em>Arkham Advertiser<\/em> with additional printing as permitted by the weather throughout the storm\u2019s duration. Listen for instructions and refrain from taking any unnecessary risks through the duration of the flooding. Above all, your life and well-being matter most.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><a href=\"https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/2025\/03\/The-Arkham-Advertiser-02-Fall-24.pdf\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/2025\/03\/Download-Button.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-989\" style=\"width:250px\"\/><\/a><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n<p><em>This edition of the Arkham Advertiser was first available as a show giveaway at PAX Unplugged 2024 and GAMA 2025 in the USA, and Dragonmeet 2024 in the UK. <\/em><\/p>\n","protected":false},"featured_media":1731,"parent":0,"template":"","meta":{"_acf_changed":true},"key-tag":[34,15,41,32],"class_list":["post-1809","news","type-news","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","key-tag-aconyte","key-tag-card-games","key-tag-ffg","key-tag-novels"],"acf":[],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO Premium plugin v22.3 (Yoast SEO v22.9) - https:\/\/yoast.com\/wordpress\/plugins\/seo\/ -->\n<title>Breaking News: Miskatonic Flood Alert | ArkhamHorror.com | The Official Arkham Horror Website News<\/title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/news\/breaking-news-miskatonic-flood-alert\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Breaking News: Miskatonic Flood Alert | ArkhamHorror.com | The Official Arkham Horror Website News\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Breaking news from the Arkham Advertiser: read it on ArkhamHorror.com now.\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/news\/breaking-news-miskatonic-flood-alert\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"ArkhamHorror.com | The Official Arkham Horror Website\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:publisher\" content=\"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/ArkhamHorrorOfficial\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2025-04-01T17:30:29+00:00\